From 70d69e5f642b207a644fa6728106ea5a6ad17ed4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans Bihs <hans.bihs@ntnu.no>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:47:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] curvgrid P5c: 6DOF bodies on curvilinear, mesh refinement and
 multi-block grids

- grid_locate.cpp: point location on the curvilinear grid (geo_quad, geo_cell, geo_cells, geo_box),
  geo_width, geo_grad, cellarea; lexer::curv_logical (global logical coordinates of a physical point)
- NHFLOW 6DOF (X 10 1, 2, 3, X 350) on G 50: the hull on the sigma grid by the physical cell centres,
  forcing normals and widths, loads by bilinear interpolation and geo_cell ownership, surface integrals
  about the hull, remeshing length from the mean physical width; refusals X 60 2, X 38, X 13, X 320
- SFLOW 6DOF (X 10 2, 3) on G 50: the waterline level set by the exact distance to the waterline
- mesh refinement: zone flags by the physical centres, finest_rank/finest_at by logical ranges,
  SFLOW ship fields on curvilinear patches
- multi-block: NHFLOW X 10 1/2 and SFLOW X 10 2/3 on the blocks (body on the blocks, triangle
  ownership native/block piece, per-point load sampling, initial draft depression)
- tools/sixdof_curvilinear t1-t3; 7 new regression cases
- defaults: no-LTO A/B against 12438ab: 297 cases bitwise identical

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Daw6u1EYTTxzeNU2vrWRnY
